| `as name` binds an object. A module has no names to put in it — that went
| with `export` — so it is empty, and a field off it answers null the way any
| missing field does. `as` is kept because it still says which module a
| native `emit` goes to, and one spelling everywhere is worth more than a
| refusal here.
link "modules/shared_values" as shared

assert shared = {}
assert shared ∈ Object
assert shared.greeting = null
